<script lang="ts">
	import { examples } from '../../utils/examples'
</script>

<template>
	<DocsPage
		locale="en"
		title="Page structure"
		description="Page, PageHeader, Header and Footer: the frame of a site, with native HTML and a single main."
	>
		<h2 id="page">UIPage</h2>
		<p>
			It paints a single focusable
			<code>main</code>
			and the link that skips to it, and keeps
			<code>sidebar</code>
			and
			<code>aside</code>
			in fixed columns while scrolling. At 75rem it hides
			<code>aside</code>
			and at 54rem it hides
			<code>sidebar</code>
			and shows
			<code>bar</code>
			, where the
			<MeekoLink to="/overlays">UIDrawer</MeekoLink>
			goes. This very guide is its example: a
			<code>UIPage</code>
			cannot be nested, because a page has only one
			<code>main</code>
			.
		</p>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.page" />
		<DocsApi
			caption="UIPage props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'layout', type: 'docs | dashboard | landing', default: 'docs', description: 'Distribution of the columns.' },
				{ name: 'mainId', type: 'string', default: 'contenido', description: 'id of the main, target of the skip link.' },
				{ name: 'mainLang', type: 'string', description: 'lang of the main, if its content is in another language.' },
				{ name: 'skipLabel', type: 'string', description: 'Text of the skip link. The default value follows the language of the document.' },
				{ name: 'class / lang / dir', type: 'HTML attributes', description: 'They reach the root.' },
			]"
		/>
		<p>
			Its snippets are
			<code>default</code>
			,
			<code>header</code>
			,
			<code>notices</code>
			,
			<code>bar</code>
			,
			<code>sidebar</code>
			,
			<code>aside</code>
			and
			<code>footer</code>
			.
			<code>notices</code>
			goes under the header, with the width of the page, and takes no room when its content paints nothing.
		</p>
		<h2 id="page-header">UIPageHeader</h2>
		<p>
			The title of a page, with its description, breadcrumb and actions. It is the only
			<code>h1</code>
			: the one of this guide is one.
		</p>
		<DocsApi
			caption="UIPageHeader props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'title', type: 'string', description: 'Required. The h1.' },
				{ name: 'description', type: 'string', description: 'Text under the title.' },
				{ name: 'layout', type: 'docs | dashboard | landing', default: 'docs', description: 'Size of the title.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<p>
			It accepts the
			<code>breadcrumb</code>
			,
			<code>actions</code>
			and
			<code>default</code>
			snippets.
		</p>
		<h2 id="header">UIHeader and UIFooter</h2>
		<p>
			The header has a fixed height,
			<code>--ui-header-height</code>
			. On narrow screens its links move to a menu with
			<code>popover</code>
			, which floats and does not move the page. A
			<code>brand</code>
			image declares
			<code>width</code>
			and
			<code>height</code>
			to reserve its space.
		</p>
		<div class="docs-grid">
			<UIHeader
				label="Sample header"
				menuLabel="Sample menu"
				current="#header"
				bind:sticky="false"
				bind:brand="{ name: 'Meeko', href: '#header' }"
				bind:items="[
					{ label: 'Guide', href: '#header' },
					{ label: 'API', href: '#page' },
				]"
			>
				<snippet name="actions"><UIButton size="sm">Sign in</UIButton></snippet>
			</UIHeader>
			<UIFooter
				label="Sample footer"
				description="Typed components for Meeko."
				bind:brand="{ name: 'Meeko', href: '#header' }"
				bind:groups="[
					{ title: 'Product', items: [{ label: 'Guide', href: '#header' }] },
					{ title: 'Community', items: [{ label: 'GitHub', href: 'https://github.com/meekojs/meeko' }] },
				]"
			/>
		</div>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.header" />
		<DocsApi
			caption="UIHeader props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'brand', type: 'UIBrand', description: 'name, product, image and target of the brand.' },
				{ name: 'items', type: 'readonly UINavigationLink[]', description: 'The links: label and href or to.' },
				{ name: 'current', type: 'string', description: 'The current link, when they use href.' },
				{ name: 'label / menuLabel', type: 'string', description: 'Name of the navigation and of the menu button.' },
				{ name: 'sticky', type: 'boolean', default: 'true', description: 'Keeps the header fixed while scrolling.' },
				{ name: 'size', type: 'UIContainerSize', default: '2xl', description: 'Maximum width.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<p>
			It accepts the
			<code>brand</code>
			,
			<code>nav</code>
			,
			<code>actions</code>
			and
			<code>menu</code>
			snippets.
		</p>
		<DocsApi
			caption="UIFooter props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'brand / description', type: 'UIBrand / string', description: 'The brand and its text.' },
				{ name: 'groups', type: 'readonly UIFooterGroup[]', description: 'Columns of links: title and items.' },
				{ name: 'items', type: 'readonly UINavigationLink[]', description: 'Loose links.' },
				{ name: 'label', type: 'string', description: 'Name of the navigation.' },
				{ name: 'size', type: 'UIContainerSize', default: '2xl', description: 'Maximum width.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<p>
			It accepts the
			<code>brand</code>
			,
			<code>about</code>
			,
			<code>actions</code>
			and
			<code>legal</code>
			snippets. The types
			<code>UIPageProps</code>
			,
			<code>UIPageHeaderProps</code>
			,
			<code>UIHeaderProps</code>
			,
			<code>UIFooterProps</code>
			and
			<code>UIBrand</code>
			are exported from
			<code>@meekojs/ui/runtime</code>
			.
		</p>
	</DocsPage>
</template>
